From: inFAMOUS FoB Recomp contributors
Subject: [PATCH 0015] video: support decoded RSX texture formats, resolve feedback sampling and prevent cutscene composite overwrite

- Whitelist all decoded RSX texture formats (16-bit packed, HILO normal maps, depth, 32-bit floats)
  in d3d12_bind_texture and render_frame prepass to eliminate NULL SRV drops on props and surfaces.
- Snapshot active render target into a dedicated multi-slot scratch feedback copy indexed by active
  render target slot (cur_rt / MRTs) when sampled as SRV (e.g. refraction/blending on glass bottles
  and props), eliminating D3D12 RTV/SRV hazard and multi-target scratch clobbering.
- Validate DXGI_FORMAT, dimensions, and sample count before CopyResource, and retire superseded
  feedback scratch resources through the per-frame GPU fence retirement queue (PR #11).
- Compute current batch draw composition upfront at entry of render_frame and bypass composite_present
  when no offscreen draws occur, clearing composite selection to prevent cutscene Bink video overwrite.
- Add hybrid spin-yield to cellGcmSetWaitFlip loop to reduce guest frame pacing stalls.

